# Dryas Workflow
- The user's dev workflow, called the Dryas Workflow, is documented in `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-workflow.md` (written by setup from the dryas-workflow repo). Machine-specific notes, if present: `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-local.md`. Read them before multi-step work or when asked about the workflow.
- The repo is the source of truth for these rules and that doc. Edit the repo (`claude/CLAUDE.md.template`, `docs/workflow.md`), merge, then re-run setup (`install/install.sh`, once per Claude config dir). Never hand-edit the plugin files, the copy in `~/.dryas/docs`, or these injected rules.

# Workflow rules
- Brainstorm first, always (superpowers:brainstorming). Nothing is built or dispatched before the user approves the design.
- Design work (UI/UX, layout, visual style, components, on-screen copy) uses both `ui-ux-pro-max` and `impeccable`.
- Single-file fix: plain Claude on the strong tier. Anything multi-step: `/orchestrate <task>` on the approved design.
- Every multi-step task runs in its own git worktree. One agent per worktree: never two sessions in one worktree; parallel loops each get their own worktree and branch. Merge only after `/wreview` and superpowers:verification-before-completion.
- Layers: Jev = decision support (gates, routing; never writes code or plans), Ruflo = orchestration and the only memory/learning layer, Superpowers = process.
- Hook order per event: scope lock -> Jev -> Ruflo -> observer (observe-only, last). Stages: `jev/chain.json` in the Dryas plugin folder.
- `.orchestrate/` (incl. `.orchestrate/PLAN.md`) in a worktree is orchestration scratch: globally git-ignored, never committed.
- Ask before any install, move, delete or overwrite, including any change to the account's settings.json (`$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json`, default `~/.claude/settings.json`). Show a dry-run or diff first.
- Commands: `/orchestrate`, `/wplan`, `/wreview`, `/commit` (Jev-gated, never pushes), `/tune` (weekly calibration), `/handoff` (Jev-scored context reset: run it, then `/clear`).
